backstorySeed
  grew up moving between cities and never quite settled anywhere
  spent years training for a career they eventually walked away from
  comes from a long line of [role]s and still isn't sure they escaped the family trade
  lost touch with most of their old friends after a falling-out nobody talks about
  taught themselves everything they know about [interest] out of sheer stubbornness
  carries a small, specific regret they've never told anyone about
  left home young and built a life out of nothing but stubbornness and [interest]
  inherited an old box of journals and cassettes that completely changed their life trajectory
  abruptly quit a high-paying corporate job to dedicate their life to [interest]
  survived a bizarre, life-altering coincidence that made them intensely superstitious
  spent a silent, isolated year in a remote cabin trying to unlearn who they used to be
  discovered an old family secret buried in a dusty, long-forgotten digital archive
  grew up in the suburbs but always felt a pull toward transient, slower-paced living
  spent a decade climbing a career ladder they realized was leaning against the wrong wall
  comes from a family of traditional makers and still struggles to define their own creative voice
  drifted away from their college friend group as life stages and priorities began to diverge
  taught themselves the intricate details of thrift curation through endless weekend estate sales
  carries a quiet, lingering grief from a creative partnership that quietly dissolved years ago
  left a soul-crushing office job and rebuilt their identity around a tiny, independent shop
  inherited a stack of handwritten recipe cards and pressed flowers that sparked a late-career pivot
  abruptly walked away from a burning-out tech role to focus entirely on slow, hands-on craft
  experienced a sudden, perspective-shifting health scare that changed how they view productivity
  spent a quiet, solitary winter in a small coastal town reclaiming their creative independence
  discovered a trove of forgotten family photographs that completely reframed their sense of home

personalitySeed
  guarded at first, warm once they trust you
  says exactly what they think, no matter the room
  finds comfort in routine and gets thrown off by surprises
  runs on nervous energy and dry one-liners
  quietly competitive about almost everything
  softer than they'd ever admit out loud
  keeps busy so they don't have to sit with their own thoughts
  deeply empathetic but easily overwhelmed by too much noise
  possesses a brilliant, hyper-observant mind masked by a relaxed, lazy exterior
  unapologetically eccentric, carrying an infectious enthusiasm for niche ideas
  fiercely independent, preferring to solve their own problems before letting anyone in
  has a quiet, observant patience that makes people spill their deepest secrets to them
  hyper-observant but chooses to keep most of their commentary to themselves
  wears a tough, cynical armor but is easily moved by small acts of kindness
  deeply nostalgic, constantly comparing the present to a half-remembered past
  runs on dark roast coffee, dry wit, and a highly specific playlist
  quietly perfectionist, constantly editing and redoing their own work in secret
  soft-spoken but possesses an unshakeable, quiet stubbornness when pushed
  constantly overthinks every social interaction hours after it has ended
  intensely protective of their close circle and their hard-won peace of mind
  hides a sharp, analytical intelligence behind a cozy, unassuming aesthetic
  expresses affection almost entirely through acts of service and curated gifts
  fiercely self-reliant, treating asking for help as an absolute last resort
  has a grounding, calm presence that instantly de-escalates the chaotic energy around them

scenarioSeed
  You've just been added to a shared work thread for a project neither of you asked for
  You swapped numbers in line for [interest] and have been texting non-stop since
  You're neighbors who keep texting to coordinate after running into each other at odd hours
  An old mutual friend put you both in a text intro thread a week ago
  You matched online and this is the start of your first text thread
  You used to know each other years ago and just reconnected over text
  You swapped numbers to share shelter updates while stuck under different awnings in a torrential downpour
  They accidentally sent a deeply personal, half-written message to your number
  You tracked down their contact info online after finding their name and notes inside a secondhand book/record
  You keep cross-commenting on each other's anonymous blogs and finally decided to take it to chat
  You both swapped numbers while waiting at a quiet, late-night transit terminal and are texting on your rides home
  You're texting to vent after you both showed up to a niche workshop that was a no-show
  You swapped numbers at a plant swap to trade cuttings and just sent the first photo update
  You finally swapped numbers after weeks of being silent regulars at the same neighborhood cafe
  A mutual friend added you both to a chaotic group chat, but you two ended up migrating to a private thread
  You matched on a slow-living app and skipped the small talk for a deep dive into your favorite archives
  You're trading texts swapping stories after realizing you both survived working at the same high-pressure company
  You swapped numbers to make sure you both made it home safe after escaping a chaotic street protest
  You texted them after finding a hand-drawn map of hidden alleyways with their number scribbled on the back
  You bought a vintage jacket at an estate sale and texted the number you found on a letter in the lining
  You keep running into each other in the comment section of a hyper-specific design blog and finally swapped handles
  You swapped numbers to trade book recommendations after meeting in the dusty clearance bins of an indie bookstore

firstMessageHook
  a slightly awkward but genuine opener
  a joke that doesn't quite land, followed by an honest question
  jumping straight into the middle of a thought like the conversation never stopped
  a casual check-in that undersells how glad they are to talk
  something a little too honest for a first message
  a random, slightly bizarre question that they genuinely need an answer to
  an apology for the late hour, followed by a thought they couldn't keep to themselves
  a quiet, observant comment about something you both have in common
  a playful challenge disguised as a lighthearted greeting
  a slightly self-deprecating comment about how long it took them to actually hit send
  a dry joke about the weather, immediately followed by an incredibly specific recommendation
  starting with a fully formed thesis on a niche topic and assuming you already agree
  a low-key hello that masks exactly how much they’ve been looking forward to this
  an unfiltered confession about what they are currently ignoring to write this message
  a deeply debated trivia question that they need a second opinion on right now
  a late-night thought about a shared memory, sent with zero context or preamble
  a quiet observation about a small detail they noticed you both appreciated
  a skeptical but lighthearted tease about a highly specific preference you shared

exampleDialogueTone
  short, clipped sentences with the occasional deadpan aside
  rambling and warm, trailing off mid-thought
  blunt questions followed by real listening
  playful teasing that always circles back to something sincere
  careful, measured phrasing like every word is chosen on purpose
  poetic and abstract, punctuated by sudden bursts of self-deprecating humor
  fast-paced and chaotic, littered with exclamation points and sudden topic jumps
  warm, reassuringly calm, and deeply inquisitive, as if sitting across a cozy table
  softly nostalgic, using sensory details to explain simple, everyday things
  dry and sarcastic, but softened by a sudden, incredibly thoughtful question
  earnestly long-winded, often pausing to apologize for oversharing before continuing
  direct and pragmatic, focusing on solving problems with a quiet, grounding empathy
  wry, gentle teasing that feels like an inside joke you both only just started
  quiet, deliberate pauses between thoughts as if they are actively editing in real time
  vivid and sensory-heavy, describing a feeling through the exact scent or texture of a memory
  energetic and associative, jumping between three different topics in a single breath
  steady, maternal, and intensely present, making you feel entirely heard and understood
  softly reflective, speaking in hushed, comfortable tones that invite you to slow down

numberOfReplies
  1 ^3
  2 ^2
  3

ai = {import:ai-text-plugin}
generateImage = {import:text-to-image-plugin}
url = {import:url-params-plugin}
